01:18:42.627 --> 01:18:46.208
based on that. We have to directly try to match it to what we anticipate

01:18:46.240 --> 01:18:50.270
for the cash flow. And that's where Metered could be helpful. With PTIF,

01:18:50.800 --> 01:18:54.268
it's just one portfolio for the whole state managed the same way

01:18:54.768 --> 01:18:58.074
without any thought of cash flows. So that's

01:18:58.122 --> 01:19:03.356
where a private investment manager can kind of help us ladder out those

01:19:03.856 --> 01:19:07.033
expenses. Can you maybe just give us a little bit

01:19:07.533 --> 01:19:10.963
of understanding of What the state requirements are

01:19:11.095 --> 01:19:15.219
for the— kind of how are you handcuffed?

01:19:15.267 --> 01:19:19.746
You mentioned no equities. Could you push all of the portfolio

01:19:19.876 --> 01:19:23.541
out to a 5-year duration, or do you have to keep

01:19:24.041 --> 01:19:29.311
a certain duration of the portfolio at 2 years? So there— right

01:19:29.811 --> 01:19:33.366
now there's only a final maturity of 5 years. However, with the

01:19:33.415 --> 01:19:37.081
duration portfolio, We kind of have an internal

01:19:37.225 --> 01:19:40.911
push to keep it under 3 years, arguably around the 2.5 range.

01:19:41.552 --> 01:19:44.901
The rationale for this really is liquidity. So when I say

01:19:45.401 --> 01:19:48.474
ladder portfolio, you can see you're invested a little bit in the 0 to 1

01:19:48.523 --> 01:19:51.407
year, a little bit in the 1 to 2 year, and the 2 to 3

01:19:51.907 --> 01:19:54.500
year. What this does is it kind of helps us to get the best of

01:19:54.532 --> 01:19:57.881
both worlds of investing longer term, so getting the higher 5-year

01:19:58.381 --> 01:20:02.239
yield, but at the same time, we're not putting equal come out in trouble if

01:20:02.739 --> 01:20:06.665
there does, you know, if there's an impending need to use the funds. And so

01:20:07.213 --> 01:20:10.829
with that, the 5-year minimum, or the 5-year maximum maturity

01:20:11.039 --> 01:20:15.106
set by the state of Utah, is arguably

01:20:15.219 --> 01:20:19.243
already very conservative. However, we like to keep a duration even

01:20:19.743 --> 01:20:23.118
shorter just for the sake of liquidity. Does that help answer the question? Yeah.

01:20:23.167 --> 01:20:26.568
Okay. I think so. And then my last question is,

01:20:26.748 --> 01:20:29.995
