I'd work construction so that it would be hard so I

01:48:30.778 --> 01:48:34.512
wouldn't get my feet all muddy. It doesn't freeze in the valley anymore,

01:48:35.041 --> 01:48:38.710
so your feet are always muddy. And we grew up

01:48:39.210 --> 01:48:42.539
with valley snow. It wasn't mountain snow, valley rain.

01:48:43.452 --> 01:48:46.785
It was valley snow. And it would pile up and it would

01:48:46.817 --> 01:48:50.504
be black and nasty from all the tire marks. And we all

01:48:51.004 --> 01:48:54.839
remember that. It was— I remember thinking I would freeze to

01:48:54.903 --> 01:48:58.179
death on Halloween. 30 seconds remaining.

01:48:59.576 --> 01:49:03.943
And it's just so much warmer. I've heard 4 to 7 degree temperature increase

01:49:04.457 --> 01:49:08.439
from, you know, if everything is approved and we get those gas power

01:49:08.487 --> 01:49:12.084
plants running and they use all the water. And I'm like,

01:49:12.245 --> 01:49:15.938
I remember you guys being so like, it's all renewables. You know,

01:49:15.954 --> 01:49:19.229
we can be conscious, like we're doing smart development,

01:49:19.309 --> 01:49:22.344
we're thinking of you guys, we don't want you to get cancer, we don't want

01:49:22.376 --> 01:49:25.780
you to be sick, because it's just making these people who are

01:49:25.812 --> 01:49:29.281
already rich and unhappy richer. Your time is up. I love

01:49:29.781 --> 01:49:29.859
all of you.

01:49:48.308 --> 01:49:51.728
My name is Amy Lawson, and I'm actually a resident of Tooele County,

01:49:51.840 --> 01:49:55.308
and I'm here with Tooele Cares, and we're part of a coalition

01:49:55.357 --> 01:49:58.841
that is just asking for a moratorium on any new data

01:49:59.341 --> 01:50:02.743
center across the state. So I'm here for 14B right now,

01:50:02.823 --> 01:50:06.082
asking that you say no for any new zoning that allows for a data center

01:50:06.195 --> 01:50:07.578
out here in Eagle Mountain. Thank you.

01:50:11.361 --> 01:50:12.938
That's all I have.

01:50:14.880 --> 01:50:16.274
Okay. Would you like to speak?

01:50:19.300 --> 01:50:22.570
State your name. And he emailed a form in, double-check.

01:50:22.634 --> 01:50:25.095
If not, we'll get one filled out after.

01:50:25.820 --> 01:50:28.478
Yep. Uh, Jay Johnson. Janelle Smith.

01:50:29.381 --> 01:50:33.429
Uh, we're residents on Lake Mountain. I'm here tonight because Lake

01:50:33.929 --> 01:50:37.037
Mountain Road has transformed into a high-speed commuter shortcut.

01:50:38.160 --> 01:50:41.383
Every single weekday between 5:00 AM and 7:00

01:50:41.883 --> 01:50:45.248
AM, 4:00 PM and 6:00 PM, the street

01:50:45.748 --> 01:50:49.466
sees thousands of drivers cutting through at high speeds directly past

01:50:49.966 --> 01:50:53.732
front yards and family homes. This volume and speed

01:50:54.232 --> 01:50:57.677
creates a severe safety hazard on a narrow residential road.

01:50:57.870 --> 01:51:01.237
that was never designed to handle shift

01:51:01.285 --> 01:51:04.944
change commuter traffic. Most critically, it has made

01:51:05.444 --> 01:51:09.269
the crossing of the street extremely dangerous. I'm asking the city

01:51:09.769 --> 01:51:11.144
to take action through 3 steps.

01:51:12.770 --> 01:51:16.877
Protect the children, the people that cross it, the animals.

01:51:17.876 --> 01:51:21.468
Install a high visibility crosswalk at the 3 intersections.

01:51:22.870 --> 01:51:26.910
Thank you. with flashing beacons if possible, and then temporary

01:51:27.410 --> 01:51:30.325
speed cushions to force commuters to slow down.

01:51:32.032 --> 01:51:34.121
Implement traffic calming signage,

01:51:35.776 --> 01:51:39.394
temporary radar so the speeders know how fast they're going,

01:51:40.420 --> 01:51:43.327
and possibly stop signs at the multiple intersections.

01:51:44.894 --> 01:51:48.576
The other is to target peak hour enforcement, which has

01:51:49.042 --> 01:51:52.294
been happening, station traffic enforcement

01:51:52.567 --> 01:51:55.046
on Lake Mountain Road during critical shift change windows.

01:51:56.292 --> 01:51:59.969
I've seen everything from 40 to 80 miles

01:52:00.002 --> 01:52:02.373
an hour. The road was graded today, which is great,

01:52:03.509 --> 01:52:06.914
but it increases traffic and speed by exponential

01:52:07.414 --> 01:52:08.609
amount. So thank you.

01:52:14.461 --> 01:52:17.045
Okay, is there anyone else here that did not get an opportunity to speak?

01:52:18.030 --> 01:52:22.130
Okay. Please state your name and

01:52:22.212 --> 01:52:23.764
fill out a form, give it to Lacey.

01:52:25.630 --> 01:52:29.562
Hi, my name is Casey Jensen. I'm here today

01:52:29.772 --> 01:52:33.695
to discuss my concern as a pedestrian of my safety.

01:52:34.599 --> 01:52:38.024
And I live not too far from

01:52:38.560 --> 01:52:40.832
Eagle Mountain Drive and Pony Express.

01:52:43.136 --> 01:52:46.922
Geez, I've gone out during peak hours and I have almost

01:52:47.422 --> 01:52:51.301
been hit by a car several times. I— all I'm asking is

01:52:51.478 --> 01:52:55.344
to invest in just pedestrian safety equipment,

01:52:56.050 --> 01:52:59.900
as multiple other residents here have discussed. I think

01:53:00.061 --> 01:53:03.349
a streetlight near Shadow Drive would be an excellent idea too.

01:53:04.552 --> 01:53:08.258
Also, there's a discussion about another

01:53:08.758 --> 01:53:12.599
resident moving here due to lower volume

01:53:13.099 --> 01:53:16.481
of traffic. And I wholeheartedly believe that

01:53:16.966 --> 01:53:20.609
investing in public transportation will relieve an

01:53:21.109 --> 01:53:21.959
immense amount of that traffic.

01:53:22.441 --> 01:53:25.928
And I believe that

01:53:26.217 --> 01:53:30.015
high volume of traffic also deters new buyers and new money coming into

01:53:30.515 --> 01:53:33.046
the city. I believe that's all. Thank you.

01:53:37.908 --> 01:53:41.193
Is there anyone else that we missed? Gentleman here.

01:53:41.517 --> 01:53:41.776
Okay.

01:53:50.930 --> 01:53:54.996
My name is Jacinto Moreno, and I'm here concerning the—

01:53:55.952 --> 01:54:00.492
oh, geez— the Corgan Farms data

01:54:00.992 --> 01:54:04.758
center. I'm just concerned

01:54:05.258 --> 01:54:08.904
with our current data center, the Meta, and its power consumption

01:54:09.001 --> 01:54:11.540
being around 133 megawatts.

01:54:13.092 --> 01:54:17.086
The power consumption and the heat from that, along with the CO2

01:54:22.080 --> 01:54:25.811
just kind of are worrying me as a citizen. I think that's a great question.

01:54:26.506 --> 01:54:30.061
as well as the expansion of the metadata center, adding more

01:54:30.561 --> 01:54:33.826
commuters and jobs for, uh,

01:54:33.842 --> 01:54:35.001
people in Eagle Mountain.

01:54:38.157 --> 01:54:41.498
I just think the concern should

01:54:41.998 --> 01:54:45.920
be brought towards that. Um, but that

01:54:48.910 --> 01:54:49.635
Thanks.

01:54:52.402 --> 01:54:55.721
Anyone else that I've missed? Okay,

01:54:55.769 --> 01:54:59.409
seeing no one, we will close the public comment

01:54:59.457 --> 01:55:03.289
period at 7:21 and bring it back to the council.

01:55:03.706 --> 01:55:07.282
Time's been set aside for the council to make comments, and we'll

01:55:07.314 --> 01:55:09.238
start with Councilmember Clark.

01:55:10.665 --> 01:55:14.369
Thank you, Mayor. Um, it's good to see so many faces here, uh, some new

01:55:14.869 --> 01:55:18.634
faces and some old friendly faces. And I see a former council

01:55:19.134 --> 01:55:21.473
member sitting out there in the front row, and It's good to see you.

01:55:23.570 --> 01:55:32.234
I am so— I've

01:55:32.282 --> 01:55:35.885
been thinking a lot about the concerns that people have about

01:55:35.917 --> 01:55:39.167
the things that we're doing as a city. And I think it's

01:55:39.232 --> 01:55:42.562
really important for you guys to feel like you can reach out and talk

01:55:43.062 --> 01:55:47.705
to us because our packet this week for our city council meeting was 749

01:55:47.802 --> 01:55:51.063
pages. which means that we get it on Thursday night,

01:55:51.770 --> 01:55:53.891
and we need to prepare and read it,

01:55:54.662 --> 01:55:58.521
and try to figure out what the residents

01:55:59.021 --> 01:56:02.639
of our community want us to do with the decisions that are being proposed

01:56:02.655 --> 01:56:04.399
in that 749 pages.

01:56:07.196 --> 01:56:10.167
Our community is growing,

01:56:11.170 --> 01:56:14.846
and there's lots of things that are happening, and it makes it really difficult

01:56:15.346 --> 01:56:19.389
sometimes to be able to reach out to all 80,000 residents. But that doesn't mean

01:56:19.405 --> 01:56:23.642
that we're going to stop trying. We continuously work with our comms

01:56:23.690 --> 01:56:27.863
team and our staff here at the city. We try to make ourselves available

01:56:28.891 --> 01:56:32.036
on social media and via phone calls and different things like that so that you

01:56:32.536 --> 01:56:35.936
guys have access to us. And earlier

01:56:36.436 --> 01:56:39.724
this year, we were doing neighborhood listening sessions where we'd come

01:56:40.224 --> 01:56:44.122
to different neighborhoods and invite you to just come and share your concerns and

01:56:44.138 --> 01:56:47.235
your ideas and your hopes and

01:56:47.735 --> 01:56:51.363
dreams. So I think the thing that I want to stress more than anything is

01:56:53.253 --> 01:56:57.248
we work for you, and we get that. We know that it's a sacrifice

01:56:57.378 --> 01:57:00.781
for us to do that, and it's not meant to be something that we

01:57:01.281 --> 01:57:04.348
do forever. We spend time away from

01:57:04.848 --> 01:57:08.474
our families doing this, but we do it because we believe in the system

01:57:08.974 --> 01:57:12.809
where people elect people that share their values and

01:57:13.472 --> 01:57:17.342
go and vote on their behalf. So I just want to kind of reshape

01:57:17.842 --> 01:57:21.211
and reframe that. I also want to thank our staff for all

01:57:21.259 --> 01:57:24.326
that they do. We're losing a staff member

01:57:24.855 --> 01:57:28.709
next week, and, um, he's a really incredible

01:57:29.209 --> 01:57:32.193
staff member, just like a lot of our staff members. So I don't want to,

01:57:32.257 --> 01:57:35.709
like, outshine too much, but because he's leaving, I just want

01:57:36.209 --> 01:57:40.258
to say, David, thank you. Thank you for the tenacity And

01:57:40.436 --> 01:57:44.828
the excitement that you brought to a

01:57:45.328 --> 01:57:48.198
really boring topic of engineering.

01:57:49.209 --> 01:57:52.703
And we're really grateful for the things that we were able to accomplish

01:57:53.203 --> 01:57:55.551
as a city with your help. So thank you for all that you do,

01:57:55.615 --> 01:57:58.501
and we wish you the best in your next chapter of life.

01:58:01.127 --> 01:58:04.391
Thanks, Mayor. Welcome, everyone. It's good to see you. It's always nice to see

01:58:04.891 --> 01:58:08.587
some of— so many smiling faces and Eagle Mountain residents. and those who are outside

01:58:09.087 --> 01:58:13.195
of our community. Ben, it's good to see you again. Thanks and welcome for—

01:58:13.323 --> 01:58:16.567
welcome back to the chamber. That side's a little more comfortable

01:58:16.615 --> 01:58:20.212
than this side, I think. I'll just

01:58:20.712 --> 01:58:23.696
say it that way. I too just want to— I just want to express my

01:58:23.760 --> 01:58:27.132
gratitude to David Salazar, recognize the contributions he's made

01:58:27.632 --> 01:58:31.130
to our city, in particular as we have been working through transportation engineering plans

01:58:31.630 --> 01:58:34.905
with him. And all of our staff members work as

01:58:35.003 --> 01:58:38.304
hard as he does. The turkey thinks he needs to live in

01:58:38.321 --> 01:58:41.929
a warmer climate because that's what his wife grew up in. And so I

01:58:42.285 --> 01:58:45.309
wish him and his family the very best in their new adventures.

01:58:46.812 --> 01:58:49.189
And the mayor gave me permission to share this, so I'm going to share it.

01:58:49.238 --> 01:58:53.321
We've— and I'm excited about this. I don't

01:58:53.821 --> 01:58:56.452
know if the council members all know this. I know some of them just heard

01:58:56.952 --> 01:59:00.802
me speaking about this earlier, but we We've secured a gentleman

01:59:00.850 --> 01:59:03.498
who's agreed to come work for the City of Eagle Mountain to do the job

01:59:03.998 --> 01:59:07.398
that Todd Black was doing. His name is Justin Dodd,

01:59:08.152 --> 01:59:11.539
and I'm really looking forward to him coming and serving our community.

01:59:11.587 --> 01:59:15.070
He's due to arrive middle of November. He's a Wyoming

01:59:15.118 --> 01:59:18.873
Fish and Game biologist and right now a conservation

01:59:18.889 --> 01:59:22.838
officer, and he has some military background. And so I just

01:59:23.338 --> 01:59:26.707
think he's going to be a really beautiful fit. And I was privileged to

01:59:26.755 --> 01:59:30.030
sit in some of the interview processes. I was invited to do that by

01:59:30.063 --> 01:59:33.370
the mayor and some of our staff members. And Brandon's

01:59:33.870 --> 01:59:37.047
shaking his head. He sat in those meetings, he and Brad and Steve and

01:59:37.547 --> 01:59:42.009
myself and others. And it was— he's

01:59:42.509 --> 01:59:45.637
the right man for the job. And I couldn't be more excited for the gentleman

01:59:45.702 --> 01:59:48.801
who's going to get to come try and fill some very, very big shoes in

01:59:48.929 --> 01:59:52.764
Todd Black's. Thank you. Todd Black's former position. So I'm grateful

01:59:52.780 --> 01:59:56.601
for that. Welcome, and I look forward to the dialogue that we'll have

01:59:56.650 --> 01:59:57.039
this evening.

02:00:00.637 --> 02:00:04.131
Welcome. It's happy for me to see as many of you as are here.

02:00:04.743 --> 02:00:08.076
We love it when you reach out to us, and we can— we need your

02:00:08.108 --> 02:00:11.222
eyes and ears to notify us of things that we might not be aware of.

02:00:11.287 --> 02:00:14.787
Like, Jay, thanks for talking about Lake Mountain Road. That's— I

02:00:15.287 --> 02:00:18.951
know we just We just concluded a speed study where numerous streets were

02:00:19.641 --> 02:00:22.355
studied, and I don't think Lake Mountain Road was one of those.

02:00:22.644 --> 02:00:24.940
So, but that would be one that we'd want to get, I think, on a

02:00:25.116 --> 02:00:28.874
future study for sure. And I'm excited

02:00:29.374 --> 02:00:32.454
to have the review later of the speed study results, and it's something the council

02:00:32.954 --> 02:00:37.319
is taking super seriously and dedicating money towards solving these

02:00:37.819 --> 02:00:42.296
issues. So thank you for bringing that to our attention. Thank you. I just

02:00:42.796 --> 02:00:46.050
wanted to let people know about a teen trunk-or-treat that is being put on by

02:00:46.550 --> 02:00:50.285
the Eagle Mountain Youth City Council. It's going to have horseback riding

02:00:50.317 --> 02:00:54.088
and dancing. There will be a costume contest, a pumpkin carving

02:00:54.588 --> 02:00:56.751
contest. It's free.

02:00:57.441 --> 02:01:00.232
You would need to bring your own pre-carved pumpkin.

02:01:01.564 --> 02:01:05.206
It's the 22nd of October from 6:30 PM to 8:30

02:01:05.238 --> 02:01:08.016
PM at 2440 41 East Cedar Drive.

02:01:08.674 --> 02:01:10.956
And so it should be a lot of fun. There's a lot of energy right

02:01:11.456 --> 02:01:14.523
now with the Youth City Council, and they're doing a lot of great things,

02:01:14.555 --> 02:01:16.773
and this should be one of those. So let your teens know about that,

02:01:16.966 --> 02:01:19.140
have them come, and it should be a great, great time.

02:01:22.698 --> 02:01:26.227
Thanks for being here. It's good to see so many people here.

02:01:26.292 --> 02:01:30.116
I think— I don't know what you're all here for, but I'm

02:01:30.180 --> 02:01:33.592
glad you're here. I hope that you have some input that you can share with

02:01:34.092 --> 02:01:35.674
us when the opportunity comes.

02:01:37.758 --> 02:01:41.293
I appreciate the people who have reached out to me one-on-one. I want to

02:01:41.309 --> 02:01:46.109
make sure that I say that because I think we have

02:01:46.609 --> 02:01:50.004
a real desire to tell the truth about everything.

02:01:50.776 --> 02:01:54.043
It's really hard to do that on Facebook. I think

02:01:54.543 --> 02:01:57.326
that's an avenue that's become pretty disappointing in dialogue.

02:01:58.502 --> 02:02:01.282
I appreciate the people who have reached out, who I've had telephone calls with,

02:02:01.770 --> 02:02:05.314
that have reached out to me through direct messaging, that have reached out

02:02:05.349 --> 02:02:05.997
to me through texts.

02:02:08.755 --> 02:02:12.339
There isn't anything to hide. I love being able to talk to you and be

02:02:12.839 --> 02:02:16.390
able to tell you the reasons why I've come to the conclusions

02:02:16.423 --> 02:02:19.653
that I've come to as a council member, why I voted the way that I

02:02:20.153 --> 02:02:23.786
voted. And most of you who know me know that there really isn't anything to

02:02:24.286 --> 02:02:27.028
hide with me. It's what you see is what you get with me.

02:02:27.557 --> 02:02:31.329
Um, I appreciate you being here because I think we make way

02:02:31.345 --> 02:02:35.004
better decisions when the people who live in the areas are telling us

02:02:35.581 --> 02:02:39.321
what we can't see. It's a big city. I mean, it's 54 square

02:02:39.353 --> 02:02:43.766
miles. We, we can't see everything, and we don't know impacts

02:02:43.846 --> 02:02:47.168
of everything. Uh, sometimes we are a little bit 2D,

02:02:47.955 --> 02:02:52.236
and we need you to kind of bring the 3D world into our

02:02:52.252 --> 02:02:55.101
city hall here and let us know what are the impacts, what are we missing,

02:02:55.150 --> 02:02:57.955
how can we do better. So when you come and you share those things,

02:02:58.378 --> 02:03:01.875
I take notes every single time so that there's some things we can talk about,

02:03:01.891 --> 02:03:05.071
get some follow-up on those. Thank you for

02:03:05.571 --> 02:03:09.016
bringing that in about the lamp. I think that safety

02:03:09.064 --> 02:03:11.699
is a big deal to me. I care about the people who live here.

02:03:11.748 --> 02:03:14.796
That's why I'm doing this, and I'll be very happy to be done with it

02:03:15.296 --> 02:03:17.962
at some point. Thank you. But I want to make sure that when I'm done,

02:03:18.479 --> 02:03:21.631
that I left a mark with— we did things to make it better for the

02:03:22.131 --> 02:03:25.091
people living here. We made it safer for the people living here, and we made

02:03:25.591 --> 02:03:29.007
it possible for people to live here and not hate the existence

02:03:29.507 --> 02:03:34.252
of being here because of traffic or because of industries that are

02:03:34.752 --> 02:03:37.892
not compatible with the lifestyle that we've all carved out here. So thanks for being

02:03:37.908 --> 02:03:41.259
here. Thank you.

02:03:41.340 --> 02:03:44.666
And I would just echo, Dave Salazar has been an awesome streets

02:03:45.166 --> 02:03:48.476
engineer. I don't know any different. He's going to be very

02:03:48.540 --> 02:03:52.181
difficult to replace. He's very adept and in tune with

02:03:52.229 --> 02:03:56.159
the traffic within our city and the flow. And we're just

02:03:57.202 --> 02:04:00.859
working hard to improve traffic because we all are dealing with that.

02:04:02.190 --> 02:04:05.752
I wanted to— I also appreciate those who have reached out to me individually.

02:04:05.944 --> 02:04:10.772
There's kind of this hierarchy of— I don't

02:04:10.820 --> 02:04:14.367
know what you would call it— success. of getting something actually done,

02:04:14.400 --> 02:04:16.024
like a streetlight is a great example.

02:04:17.468 --> 02:04:21.622
At the very base level, you have like a Facebook complaint. You know,

02:04:21.849 --> 02:04:24.640
this road sucks. Fix it, City Council.

02:04:25.346 --> 02:04:27.169
It's like, I don't— okay.

02:04:28.976 --> 02:04:32.348
Then there is like an email that's well-worded.

02:04:33.268 --> 02:04:36.769
Then there's coming here, taking time out of your night to make

02:04:37.269 --> 02:04:40.593
a public comment where I can actually see a face and somebody who's being impacted.

02:04:40.658 --> 02:04:44.039
Thank you. And then there's maybe taking a city council member out to where

02:04:44.539 --> 02:04:48.281
you're talking about and showing us and seeing those, those, those types of activities.

02:04:48.859 --> 02:04:52.571
I know they require energy and effort, but it makes such a big

02:04:52.587 --> 02:04:56.346
difference. On the Williams Energy, the gentleman

02:04:56.846 --> 02:04:58.708
that, that brought that up, that's, uh,

02:04:59.897 --> 02:05:02.998
I've been out there. I've been to the site. I've walked through where the 17

02:05:03.095 --> 02:05:07.080
turbines are going to be going. It's a 289-megawatt

02:05:07.708 --> 02:05:10.406
project that is intended to power 3 data centers.

02:05:12.300 --> 02:05:16.151
Meta has kind of hit capacity with their green

02:05:16.361 --> 02:05:19.906
energy initiative with Rocky Mountain Power. Rocky Mountain Power has basically said we don't

02:05:20.406 --> 02:05:23.818
have any more solar credits or power to sell you,

02:05:23.932 --> 02:05:27.313
and so Meta will be powering those 3 data centers through nat gas.

02:05:27.993 --> 02:05:29.988
But I do have concerns about air quality.

02:05:31.497 --> 02:05:34.729
I think we need to be careful about the message that we're sending to the

02:05:35.229 --> 02:05:38.414
market of what kind of power will be okay within our city.

02:05:38.528 --> 02:05:42.348
We've recently passed an alternative energy overlay zone that

02:05:42.396 --> 02:05:45.091
will allow for geothermal, natural gas,

02:05:45.335 --> 02:05:48.992
nuclear. I don't know that we only want to settle on natural

02:05:49.492 --> 02:05:50.666
gas as the only option.

02:05:53.730 --> 02:05:56.207
I struggle with that and trying to find the balance.

02:05:57.390 --> 02:06:00.697
Cities cost money. The more homes that we

02:06:00.779 --> 02:06:03.800
add, to the city, the more cars we add, the more streets

02:06:04.300 --> 02:06:07.572
engineers that we need, and that increases taxes. How do

02:06:08.072 --> 02:06:11.842
we balance out commercial? We're not on I-15. We're not

02:06:12.548 --> 02:06:16.368
on the way to anywhere. And data centers happen

02:06:16.400 --> 02:06:20.670
to be interested in coming here. There will be roughly $3

02:06:21.170 --> 02:06:24.507
million that will be generated from the Williams plant,

02:06:24.988 --> 02:06:28.295
and that has a direct offset to costs in the city to

02:06:28.359 --> 02:06:32.068
build roads. Thank you. So the thing that I'm always struggling to

02:06:32.568 --> 02:06:35.764
balance is the quality of life in Eagle Mountain and at the same

02:06:35.861 --> 02:06:40.879
time not having to go back and ask residents

02:06:42.959 --> 02:06:46.265
for increased property taxes. How do you balance that

02:06:46.765 --> 02:06:50.334
in a city? It's just, it's a struggle. It's something that we're

02:06:50.398 --> 02:06:53.969
working through. But I appreciate those that came

02:06:54.081 --> 02:06:58.318
and made made a comment. And Jay, I would love to, to come and sit

02:06:58.818 --> 02:07:01.623
out on Lake Mountain Boulevard. I think those are great ideas, and you came with

02:07:02.123 --> 02:07:05.844
some suggestions, so that, that's a positive. Appreciate everyone coming tonight.

02:07:05.924 --> 02:07:06.215
Thank you.

02:07:10.117 --> 02:07:13.997
Perfect. I had earlier— I'm going

02:07:14.497 --> 02:07:18.241
to start at the top of this— I talked to Officer Gilstrap earlier today,

02:07:18.964 --> 02:07:21.419
and I thought he was going to come, but I haven't seen him yet because

02:07:21.919 --> 02:07:25.163
I think he was dropping his daughter off, but he sent me some numbers and

02:07:25.663 --> 02:07:29.634
I'll bet he shows up in a minute. But I had asked

02:07:30.134 --> 02:07:33.352
him about Lake Mountain Road specifically, and I

02:07:33.368 --> 02:07:36.780
don't see Officer Knutson here either, but I asked him

02:07:37.280 --> 02:07:40.920
to go over there and do some, uh, some enforcement.

02:07:41.310 --> 02:07:43.975
Had 46 traffic stops in— Where?

02:07:46.142 --> 02:07:49.852
Oh, there he is. I was just talking about some statistics

02:07:50.352 --> 02:07:52.735
that Officer Gilstrap had given me, and now I'm going to ask him to come

02:07:52.768 --> 02:07:54.890
up here and tell me what it's been like out there on the road.

02:07:57.095 --> 02:07:57.387
So, um,

02:08:00.770 --> 02:08:04.104
great timing. Did you have fun? As fun as

02:08:04.169 --> 02:08:07.227
I'll ever have. So specifically on Lake Mountain Road,

02:08:07.420 --> 02:08:10.723
I've asked you a couple weeks ago to spend some time out

02:08:11.223 --> 02:08:14.142
there and I think you spent 3 or 4 shifts with a couple of different

02:08:14.642 --> 02:08:18.651
guys. Give us some of the statistics. Yeah, we've done multiple shifts

02:08:19.151 --> 02:08:22.100
on Lake Mountain Road since we were apprised of the issue 2 weeks ago.

02:08:22.742 --> 02:08:26.432
In the 2-week time period, our CAD system shows that we've made 46

02:08:26.932 --> 02:08:31.133
traffic stops on Lake Mountain Road. Most of those have been citable offenses

02:08:31.390 --> 02:08:34.679
well over the posted speed limit. We've recognized that there's a

02:08:35.179 --> 02:08:39.007
lot of traffic that overflows off of Pony Express onto Lake Mountain,

02:08:39.685 --> 02:08:43.450
and we've been trying to address it appropriately as needs arise, which has

02:08:43.482 --> 02:08:46.552
been needed just about every morning between 4 and 6 AM.

02:08:48.815 --> 02:08:51.336
And the evenings as well, right? Oh yeah, oh yeah,

02:08:51.401 --> 02:08:54.116
traffic's real fun in Eagle Mountain mornings and evenings.

02:08:54.790 --> 02:08:57.660
Keeps us busy. So, and then the other thing that we had talked about a

02:08:57.708 --> 02:09:00.384
couple weeks ago, and I don't remember which one of you had— we're going to

02:09:00.884 --> 02:09:04.269
move the, uh, the sign over there? The speed trailer?

02:09:04.638 --> 02:09:08.010
Yeah. Yes, we're going to be moving that off of Ira Hodges over onto Lake

02:09:08.510 --> 02:09:11.510
Mountain Road. Do you know when? We've been hitting it pretty hard still,

02:09:11.687 --> 02:09:14.834
and we've been having a lot of good enforcement there, so we were planning on

02:09:15.334 --> 02:09:17.419
hitting that for probably about another week before we put the lighted sign out there.

02:09:17.949 --> 02:09:20.791
There's plenty of signage on Lake Mountain Road. There shouldn't be any excuse for the

02:09:21.291 --> 02:09:24.677
speeds. Okay. Yeah, just keep doing that for a minute, and then probably

02:09:24.709 --> 02:09:27.872
a week or two we'll see the speed trailer over there.

02:09:28.386 --> 02:09:31.672
And then also for the council, anybody up here, staff,

02:09:31.704 --> 02:09:35.087
as you're working with the— maybe I'd ask you to work with

02:09:35.520 --> 02:09:38.902
Meta specifically, is that they've designated routes and that's

02:09:39.402 --> 02:09:42.846
not a designated route. The problem is, is the subs. Every day it's

02:09:43.346 --> 02:09:45.956
a different sub and they don't necessarily know. But if we could get them to

02:09:46.261 --> 02:09:49.355
help us with their subs to use the designated routes,

02:09:49.723 --> 02:09:52.609
that is not the best route to use in a rural area.

02:09:53.170 --> 02:09:56.669
And the traffic Do you know the, like, car count? If you stop 46 cars,

02:09:56.717 --> 02:10:00.523
it's— Well, the car count, as soon as we clear a traffic stop, we're ready

02:10:00.539 --> 02:10:03.927
for the next one. So the— it's, it's pretty consistent with the

02:10:04.427 --> 02:10:08.439
speeds. Uh, we've noticed that different vehicle makers on their mapping

02:10:08.939 --> 02:10:11.939
system like to try to designate Lake Mountain Road as a 55-mile-an-hour zone,

02:10:12.533 --> 02:10:15.696
so that way we've had a lot of speeds up in that range. That's been

02:10:15.985 --> 02:10:20.144
swiftly corrected, and we've also provided some updates to safety

02:10:20.644 --> 02:10:23.885
staff down at QTS about their employees driving that speed.

02:10:25.202 --> 02:10:28.654
Perfect. Well, thank you for the update. You're welcome. Appreciate you coming down.

02:10:29.938 --> 02:10:33.214
So that was— I talked to him earlier and I thought it was just

02:10:33.714 --> 02:10:36.762
going to be easier for him to tell us what he's been experiencing. But we'll

02:10:37.262 --> 02:10:40.792
continue to help do what we can on Lake Mountain Road and try

02:10:41.292 --> 02:10:44.405
if we can't correct the traffic patterns. Also,

02:10:45.673 --> 02:10:49.891
I get to sit on our MAG board and work on transportation and funding,

02:10:49.924 --> 02:10:53.068
and it's an uphill battle and it's a heavy lift.

02:10:53.372 --> 02:10:56.982
And I'm telling you, we have had some huge victories at MAG in Eagle

02:10:57.482 --> 02:11:00.912
Mountain in the last few months, and I couldn't have done it myself.

02:11:01.553 --> 02:11:03.607
As much as I get to go down there and take credit and kind of

02:11:03.639 --> 02:11:07.232
do the final voting, that guy over there has set us up

02:11:07.732 --> 02:11:10.986
for some huge success. And I just hope we can get somebody

02:11:11.002 --> 02:11:14.790
in here that can continue to helped me be successful,

02:11:15.352 --> 02:11:18.402
